# 41. IMPORTANT SAFETY NOTE

Practice user-management commands inside your own Linux virtual machine or another system where you have permission.

Be careful with commands such as:

```bash
sudo userdel -r username
```

because they can permanently remove the user's home-directory data.

Do not experiment with user deletion, privilege changes, or account modifications on production systems without authorization.

